# Future Migration Draft

This file is a draft template for a migration that requires export and import instead of an in-place datafile upgrade. It is not part of the published documentation.

## Purpose

Use this draft when a future Oracle Database image cannot start with the existing `oradata` files. In that case, users must export data from the old database, create a new database, and import the data.

## Draft Flow

> **Caution**
> A dump-and-restore migration can lose data if users skip backups or miss schemas that were not created by this project.

1. Confirm that the old database is running.

   ```bash
   docker ps
   ```

2. Start the old database if needed.

   ```bash
   local-23ai.sh start
   ```

3. Back up schemas and workspaces created by this project.

   ```bash
   local-23ai.sh backup-all
   ```

4. Manually back up any schemas or workspaces that were not created by this project.
5. Back up the `oradata` volume.

   ```bash
   source ./scripts/util/load_env.sh

   docker exec $CONTAINER_NAME bash -c "echo 'shutdown immediate;
   exit' | sqlplus / as sysdba && exit"

   docker cp $CONTAINER_NAME:/opt/oracle/oradata ./backups/oradata
   ```

6. Stop the old containers.

   ```bash
   local-23ai.sh stop
   ```

7. Remove the old `oradata` volume only after backups are verified.

   ```bash
   docker volume rm oradata
   ```

8. Create the new connection string.

   ```bash
   source ./scripts/util/load_env.sh
   echo "CONN_STRING=sys/$ORACLE_PASSWORD@23ai:1521/FREEPDB1" >./ords-secrets/conn_string.txt
   ```

9. Start the new containers.
10. Run the first-start setup script.
11. Import the exported data.
